model {
  extend basalt.poolRuntime {
    metadata {
      constraint "The image build executes both direct credential-rate-limit and bootstrap cooldown regressions alongside its submission and protocol tests. A generation HTTP submission whose write or response was observed cannot be replayed after transport loss or an empty accepted stream, including internal HTTP, model, credential and retry-round fallbacks. Submission tracking is enabled only for generation attempts, including Home execution and credits fallback; side-effect-free token-count attempts remain replayable across models and credentials. Terminal stream failures record exactly one failed result for local hooks and ephemeral Home reporting before returning, preserving the actual error scope so direct credential rate limits still cool the credential. Error envelopes are constructed with the JSON document API and remain decodable in non-stream and SSE data responses. The final selected transport records request-local evidence without replacing proxy, TLS or pool policy. Accepted response decoder failures, buffered model provider protocol validation failures and submitted POST redirect result failures are outcome-unknown. Credits fallback returns an ambiguous failure immediately across both model pools and credentials, preserving its public error instead of the earlier cooldown refusal. Header-only mutations preserve nil or NoBody and zero-length framing, recasing idempotency map keys only on the clone to avoid implicit HTTP replay. A terminal short-circuit closes the next request body. TypeSafe System One maps the typed unknown outcome to its native detail body at both public route aliases after replay is stopped, retaining status 502 and x-should-retry false; explicit native refusals retain their body and retry headers. Before output starts, other ambiguous outcomes return 502 upstream_outcome_unknown with retryable false and x-should-retry false. Locally detected incomplete SSE frames are typed as truncation, so they cannot fall through to another model or credential. Late protocol truncation retains partial output and emits an outcome-unknown error without inventing completion. Safe pre-write connection failures and definitive provider errors, including HTTP and SSE refusals, retain retry behavior. A successful HTTP status alone does not turn a definitive provider error into an ambiguous disconnect. Real loopback regressions guard both the public API and transport replay before the native source image is built. Publication still requires the actual source and compiled producers to agree on an exact reviewed serving-to-candidate source pair, preserving the existing native schema version and complete index registry. Keep the carry until an upstream release passes the same behavior, re-applying it across source updates without rolling back the release pin."
    }
  }
}
